# H2b (SOFT, quad, RUN LAST): the TIMED pass of H2 (watcher OFF), the same construction as H2a. Arms in interleaved rounds (20 timed after 4 warm-ups): a trace of 24 all-gathers on the target sub-device
# alone, on the drafter sub-device alone, and BOTH CONCURRENTLY on the two queues over the SAME fabric link (num_links 1 on each: (a) sharing a link); the same at num_links 2 (information only: the
# production gathers use both links); and (b) SEPARATE LINKS (the drafter's gathers on link 1, the target's on link 0) which needs the prepared link-offset graft
# (optimisation/ttnn-op/subdev_h/ag_link_offset.patch: the all-gather factory adds QWEN_AG_LINK_OFFSET_SD1 to the fabric link of every sub-device-1 program; no image has it built) and reads NOT-RUN here.
# PASS = the shared-link concurrent wall <= 1.1 x max(solo), every gathered tensor identical on every chip, no hang: the two sub-devices' collectives overlap with no change to tt-metal.
# FAIL-SERIALISED / FAIL-PARTIAL = they contend for the link: build the graft, mount it, and run --link-offset 1 (PASS-SEPARATE-LINKS would say the graft is required and enough).
# READ: 'SUBDEV_H2 verdict=...' with shared_ratio, shared2_ratio, separate_ratio ('-' when not run), t_ms, d_ms and bytes; the last stdout line is the JSON (kind subdev-h2).
# TIMED: pause the ARC runners. Duration (estimate): 40 min (the box below bounds the probe; the fabric step's own limit is 45).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the sub-device overlap programme (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of
# the window branch (a branch that carries optimisation/ttnn-op/subdev_h and scripts/ci/tp4_subdev_probe.py) and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the read rules and the minutes.
# C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag of the window's own image (sed -i 's/tp4-next2-1/<tag>/' *.env): this pack builds nothing, and any C2 image carries the tt-metal sub-device bindings
# it needs (the harnesses mount this checkout's files). The cards are under development: nothing here stops, starts or hands back the node agent.

C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset fabric
C2_FABRIC_PROBE=subdev
C2_FABRIC=FABRIC_1D
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=40
